###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasRandomAllocationConcealmentScore
tara-kb:hasRandomAllocationConcealmentScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                            dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                            dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                            dcterms:description """The reporting quality score assessing whether the method used to implement the random allocation sequence is described, and whether the sequence was concealed until interventions were assigned.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                            tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasRandomAllocationConcealmentScore" ;
                                            tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """(a) Is the method presented that was used to implement the random allocation sequence,

(b) with clarification as to whether the sequence was concealed until interventions were assigned?"""@en ;
                                            tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "14"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                            tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) 'Implementation' refers to how the random assignment was applied, for example, a sealed envelope containing the computer-generated group assignment placed in the patient's chart.

(b) Concealment is required to prevent foreknowledge of and introduction of bias in treatment assignment, for example, the sealed envelope with group assignment was opened after the patient passed the baseline neurological exam and received a TCM differential diagnosis."""@en ;
                                            tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 14,
  \"question\": \"(a) Is the method presented that was used to implement the random allocation sequence, (b) with clarification as to whether the sequence was concealed until interventions were assigned?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"the method used to implement the random allocation sequence is presented\",
    \"b\": \"it is clarified whether the sequence was concealed until interventions were assigned\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                            tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) the method used to implement the random allocation sequence is presented;

(b) it is clarified whether the sequence was concealed until interventions were assigned.

N = 2 when all 2 are applicable.

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-b):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Exactly 1 of N met -> Score 1 (Partial).

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011)."""@en ;
                                            tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Methods"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                            rdfs:label "(14) Random Allocation Concealment" ;
                                            skos:altLabel "14_Random_Allocation_Concealment" ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics ;
                                            rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                            rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasRandomAllocationPersonnelScore
tara-kb:hasRandomAllocationPersonnelScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                          dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                          dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                          dcterms:description """The reporting score assessing whether the article states who generated the randomization sequence, who enrolled participants, and who assigned participants to their groups.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                          tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasRandomAllocationPersonnelScore" ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """Are there statements as to

(a) who generated the allocation sequence,

(b) who enrolled participants, and

(c) who assigned participants to their groups?"""@en ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "15"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) It must specifically state the person responsible for generating the randomization.

(b) It refers to the specific person(s) responsible for consenting the participants.

(c) It refers to the person who assigned participants to their respective randomized groups; if this person also generated the randomization scheme, the authors should report how the potential for biased group assignments was addressed (e.g., randomization schedule was kept in a locked closet from “this” person)."""@en ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 15,
  \"question\": \"Are there statements as to (a) who generated the allocation sequence, (b) who enrolled participants, and (c) who assigned participants to their groups?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"the person responsible for generating the randomization is named\",
    \"b\": \"the person(s) responsible for enrolling (consenting) participants is named\",
    \"c\": \"the person who assigned participants to their groups is named\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) the person responsible for generating the randomization is named;

(b) the person(s) responsible for enrolling (consenting) participants is named;

(c) the person who assigned participants to their groups is named.

N = 3 when all 3 are applicable.

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-c):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Any count strictly between 0 and N met -> Score 1 (Partial). This applies whether 1 of 3 or 2 of 3 sub-parts are met.

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011)."""@en ;
                                          tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Methods"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                          rdfs:label "(15) Random Allocation Personnel" ;
                                          skos:altLabel "15_Random_Allocation_Personnel" ;
                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics ;
                                          rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                          rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasRandomAllocationSequencingScore
tara-kb:hasRandomAllocationSequencingScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                           dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                           dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                           dcterms:description """A reporting quality score assessing whether the method used to generate the random allocation sequence, and any restrictions (e.g., blocking, stratification), are described.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                           tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasRandomAllocationSequencingScore" ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """(a) Is the method presented that was used to generate the random allocation sequence, and

(b) if applicable, details of any restriction (e.g., blocking, stratification)?"""@en ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "13"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) Sufficient and specific information must be provided regarding the methods utilized to generate the random allocation scheme, for example, a computer-generated table. Simply stating that patients were randomly assigned is not sufficient.

(b) If randomization restrictions were utilized, for example, stratification or blocking, the methods and details must be stated."""@en ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 13,
  \"question\": \"(a) Is the method presented that was used to generate the random allocation sequence, and (b) if applicable, details of any restriction (e.g., blocking, stratification)?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"the method used to generate the random allocation sequence is presented\",
    \"b\": \"details of any randomization restriction (e.g., blocking, stratification) are given, if applicable (N/A if no randomization restrictions (e.g., blocking, stratification) were used.)\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) the method used to generate the random allocation sequence is presented;

(b) details of any randomization restriction (e.g., blocking, stratification) are given, if applicable.

N = 2 when all 2 are applicable; N is reduced by however many sub-parts are individually N/A (see below).

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-b):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Exactly 1 of N met -> Score 1 (Partial).

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011).

Sub-part N/A conditions:

(b) is N/A if no randomization restrictions (e.g., blocking, stratification) were used (interpretive extension based on the 'if applicable' phrasing in Appendix A.2)."""@en ;
                                           tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Methods"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                           rdfs:label "(13) Random Allocation Sequencing" ;
                                           skos:altLabel "13_Random_Allocation_Sequencing" ;
                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics ;
                                           rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                           rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasReportedStudyID
tara-kb:hasReportedStudyID rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                           dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                           dcterms:description "A cross-linking annotation property designed to establish a direct relational association between an information artifact representing a 'Study Publication' (such as a journal article, systematic review, or report) and the physical, operational scientific trial or investigation process (represented by the 'Research Study' class) it documents."@en ;
                           tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasReportedStudyID" ;
                           rdfs:label "Has Reported Study ID"@en ;
                           skos:altLabel "Reported_Study_ID"@en ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
                           rdfs:range <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> ;
                           rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_8223728> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasReportingPublicationID
tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                  dcterms:description "A cross-linking annotation property designed to establish a direct relational association between a Research Study (the physical, operational clinical trial or investigation process) and the publication (such as a journal article) where the study is reported." ;
                                  tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasReportingPublicationID" ;
                                  rdfs:label "Has Reporting Publication ID" ;
                                  skos:altLabel "Reporting_Publication_ID" ;
                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
                                  rdfs:range <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_8223728> ;
                                  rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> ,
                                              <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasResultsAndOutcomesMetrics
tara-kb:hasResultsAndOutcomesMetrics rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                     dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                     dcterms:description """Category D, Results and Outcome Metrics, groups the OCSI items reporting what was actually observed in the clinical trial. The OCSI items included under this category are:
- Item 18: Participants Flow and Protocol Deviation; 
- Item 19: Participants Recruitment and Followup;
- Item 20: Participants Demographics and Characteristics;
- Item 21: Participants and Intention to Treat Analysis;
- Item 22: Study Outcomes and Effect Size;
- Item 23: Subgroup and Adjusted Analyses; and
- Item 24: Adverse Events and Side Effects."""@en ;
                                     dcterms:type tara-kb:grouping ;
                                     tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasResultsAndOutcomesMetrics" ;
                                     rdfs:comment "This category is a TARA-KB organizational convention, not sourced from Hammerschlag et al. 2011 (the OCSI paper) or the CONSORT 2010 checklist. This category's members do, however, correspond closely to CONSORT's own Results and Discussion sections, distinguishing reported/executed trial content from the planned trial design and analysis content grouped under Category C."@en ;
                                     rdfs:label "Category D: Results & Outcomes Metrics" ;
                                     skos:altLabel "Category_D_Results_Outcomes_Metrics" ;
                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasOCSIItemScoringMetadata ;
                                     rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasResultsDiscussionMetrics
tara-kb:hasResultsDiscussionMetrics rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                    dcterms:description """Category E, Results Discussion Metrics, groups the OCSI items reporting how the trial results are discussed and interpreted. The OCSI items included under this category are: 
- Item 25: Trial Strengths and Limitations; 
- Item 26: Trial Generalizability; and
- Item 27: Interpretation of Results.""" ;
                                    tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasResultsDiscussionMetrics" ;
                                    rdfs:label "Category E: Results Discussion Metrics" ;
                                    skos:altLabel "Category_E_Results_Discussion_Metrics" ;
                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasOCSIItemScoringMetadata .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasSampleSizeDetails
tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                             obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., \"n=84 (42 in intervention, 42 in control)\"."@en ;
                             dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                             dcterms:description "For the final number of participants who completed the study and were analyzed."@en ;
                             tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails" ;
                             tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Sample_Size_Details\",
  \"description\": \"For the final number of participants who completed the study and were analyzed.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                             rdfs:comment "For the final number of participants who completed the study and were analyzed (e.g., \"n=84 (42 in intervention, 42 in control)\")." ;
                             rdfs:label "Sample Size Details" ;
                             skos:altLabel "Sample_Size_Details" ;
                             rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata ;
                             rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                             rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasSampleSizeDeterminationScore
tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDeterminationScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                        dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                        dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                        dcterms:description """The reporting quality score assessing whether the rationale or calculation used to determine the study's sample size is explicitly reported.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                        tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDeterminationScore" ;
                                        tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """(a) Is there a statement regarding how the sample size was determined, and

(b) if applicable, an explanation of any interim analyses and stopping rules?"""@en ;
                                        tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "12"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                        tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) It must include statements regarding estimated effect size of the intervention based on (i) previous research and (ii) estimated attrition rate. If the study was a pilot, a statement such as 'No data exists upon which to base a sample size calculation' must be included.

(b) 'Interim analysis and stopping rules' pertains to long-term trials and may not be applicable to trials of shorter duration. If authors report that interim analyses were performed, the number of assessments and statistical tests must be reported."""@en ;
                                        tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 12,
  \"question\": \"(a) Is there a statement regarding how the sample size was determined, and (b) if applicable, an explanation of any interim analyses and stopping rules?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"a statement is given on how the sample size was determined (estimated effect size and attrition rate, or an explicit rationale for omitting the calculation in a pilot study)\",
    \"b\": \"an explanation of any interim analyses and stopping rules is given, if applicable (plausibly N/A for shorter-duration trials, for which interim analyses and stopping rules may not apply.)\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                        tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) a statement is given on how the sample size was determined (estimated effect size and attrition rate, or an explicit rationale for omitting the calculation in a pilot study);

(b) an explanation of any interim analyses and stopping rules is given, if applicable.

N = 2 when all 2 are applicable; N is reduced by however many sub-parts are individually N/A (see below).

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-b):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Exactly 1 of N met -> Score 1 (Partial).

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011).

Sub-part N/A conditions:

(b) is plausibly N/A for shorter-duration trials, for which interim analyses and stopping rules may not apply (interpretive extension based on Appendix A.2's 'may not be applicable' phrasing; the source does not use the literal term N/A here)."""@en ;
                                        tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Methods"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                        rdfs:label "(12) Sample Size Determination" ;
                                        skos:altLabel "12_Sample_Size_Determination" ;
                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics ;
                                        rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                        rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasScientificBackgroundRationaleScore
tara-kb:hasScientificBackgroundRationaleScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                              dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                              dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                              dcterms:description """The reporting quality score measuring how completely the article's introduction provides scientific background and explains the rationale for the trial.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                              tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasScientificBackgroundRationaleScore" ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """(a) Is scientific background provided and

(b) is the rationale explained?"""@en ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "2"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) Scientific background pertains to the previous research and the current understanding of the disease.

(b) Rationale pertains to the justification for the trial and/or the expected effects/benefits of the treatment."""@en ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 2,
  \"question\": \"(a) Is scientific background provided and (b) is the rationale explained?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"scientific background is provided (previous research and current understanding of the disease)\",
    \"b\": \"the rationale is explained (justification for the trial and/or expected effects/benefits)\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) scientific background is provided (previous research and current understanding of the disease);

(b) the rationale is explained (justification for the trial and/or expected effects/benefits).

N = 2 when all 2 are applicable.

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-b):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Exactly 1 of N met -> Score 1 (Partial).

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011)."""@en ;
                                              tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Introduction"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                              rdfs:label "(2) Scientific Background & Rationale" ;
                                              skos:altLabel "2_Scientific_Background_Rationale" ;
                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyRationaleAndScopeMetrics ;
                                              rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                              rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasSecondaryOutcomeMeasure
tara-kb:hasSecondaryOutcomeMeasure rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                   obo:IAO_0000112 "\"Number of migraine days, visual analogue scale (VAS) for pain, physical and mental component summary scores of the 36-item short-form health survey (SF-36), change in migraine days, number of patients with acute medication, adverse events (AE)\""@en ;
                                   dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                   dcterms:description "Any additional, non-primary endpoint(s) measured to support or contextualize the primary outcome, together with its measurement instrument or method."@en ;
                                   tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasSecondaryOutcomeMeasure" ;
                                   rdfs:label "Secondary Outcome Measure" ;
                                   skos:altLabel "Secondary_Outcome_Measure" ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                      tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure ;
                                   rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                   rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasShamAcupunctureDetails
tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                  obo:IAO_0000112 "\"Non-penetrating Streitberger placebo needle applied at non-acupoint sites.\""@en ,
                                                  "\"Sham protocol details: Superficial insertion (maximum 3 mm depth) of up to six needles on either side of the upper arm, both thighs, and below both scapulae at areas where no TCM acupuncture points are known; same number and type of needles used as verum; no manual stimulation.\"" ;
                                  dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                  dcterms:description "The specific details reported for the sham or control acupuncture intervention used for comparison, describing the device and procedure used to simulate real needling."@en ;
                                  tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureDetails" ;
                                  tara-ap:hasSynonym "Control Intervention Details" ;
                                  rdfs:label "Sham Acupuncture Details" ;
                                  skos:altLabel "Sham_Acupuncture_Details" ;
                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                     tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol ;
                                  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                  rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasShamAcupunctureUsed
tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureUsed rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                               obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., 'Yes - non-penetrating needle applied at non-acupoint sites.' or 'No - no sham or placebo control arm was used.'"@en ;
                               dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                               dcterms:description "A derived-summary annotation property stating, as a clear yes/no lead-in with a concise qualifying statement, whether the study used a sham or placebo acupuncture control arm. Populated from the sham protocol details already captured under hasAcupunctureProtocol, not from an independent re-reading of the article, to avoid introducing a second, potentially inconsistent extraction/inference."@en ;
                               tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasShamAcupunctureUsed" ;
                               tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Sham_Acupuncture_Used\",
  \"description\": \"Whether the study used a sham/placebo acupuncture control arm, stated as a clear yes/no lead-in followed by a concise qualifying statement.\",
  \"normalization\": \"Prefix the entry with exactly 'Yes -' or 'No -', followed by a concise qualifying statement (one short clause). Base this entry SOLELY on the 'Sham protocol details' sub-part already produced for hasAcupunctureProtocol in this same extraction pass -- do not re-read the article or infer anything new. If that sub-part states a real sham/placebo procedure was used, write 'Yes - ' followed by a brief restatement of what made it a sham (e.g., 'Yes - non-penetrating needle applied at non-acupoint sites'). If it states no sham arm existed, write 'No - no sham or placebo control arm was used.'\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                               rdfs:label "Sham Acupuncture Used" ;
                               skos:altLabel "Sham_Acupuncture_Used" ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol ;
                               rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                               rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasSpecificObjectivesHypothesesScore
tara-kb:hasSpecificObjectivesHypothesesScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                             dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                             dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                             dcterms:description """The reporting quality score assessing whether the article states specific objectives and hypotheses to be tested.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                             tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasSpecificObjectivesHypothesesScore" ;
                                             tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """Are there statements of

(a) specific objectives and

(b) hypotheses to be tested?"""@en ;
                                             tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "10"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                             tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) If objectives are clearly implied but not specifically stated, a Yes may be scored.

(b) The actual word hypothesis or a valid substitute, for example, theory, must be used."""@en ;
                                             tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 10,
  \"question\": \"Are there statements of (a) specific objectives and (b) hypotheses to be tested?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"specific objectives are stated\",
    \"b\": \"a hypothesis to be tested is stated\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                             tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) specific objectives are stated;

(b) a hypothesis to be tested is stated.

N = 2 when all 2 are applicable.

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-b):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Exactly 1 of N met -> Score 1 (Partial).

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011)."""@en ;
                                             tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Methods"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                             rdfs:label "(10) Specific Objectives & Hypotheses" ;
                                             skos:altLabel "10_Specific_Objectives_Hypotheses" ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyRationaleAndScopeMetrics ;
                                             rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                             rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStatisticalMethodsForOutcomesScore
tara-kb:hasStatisticalMethodsForOutcomesScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                              dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                              dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                              dcterms:description """The reporting quality score assessing whether the statistical methods used to compare groups for primary outcomes, and for any additional analyses, are stated.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                              tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStatisticalMethodsForOutcomesScore" ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """(a) Were the statistical methods stated that were used to compare groups for primary outcomes?

(b) Were the statistical methods stated that were used for additional analyses such as subgroup or adjusted analyses?"""@en ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "17"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) It must specifically state the statistical methods used to compare groups for primary outcomes.

(b) If additional analyses were performed, the specific statistical methods used must be reported for full credit."""@en ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 17,
  \"question\": \"(a) Were the statistical methods stated that were used to compare groups for primary outcomes? (b) Were the statistical methods stated that were used for additional analyses such as subgroup or adjusted analyses?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"the statistical methods used to compare groups for primary outcomes are stated\",
    \"b\": \"the statistical methods used for any additional analyses (e.g., subgroup or adjusted analyses) are stated (N/A if no additional analyses (e.g., subgroup or adjusted analyses) were performed.)\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                              tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) the statistical methods used to compare groups for primary outcomes are stated;

(b) the statistical methods used for any additional analyses (e.g., subgroup or adjusted analyses) are stated.

N = 2 when all 2 are applicable; N is reduced by however many sub-parts are individually N/A (see below).

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-b):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Exactly 1 of N met -> Score 1 (Partial).

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011).

Sub-part N/A conditions:

(b) is N/A if no additional analyses (e.g., subgroup or adjusted analyses) were performed."""@en ;
                                              tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Methods"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                              rdfs:label "(17) Statistical Methods for Outcomes" ;
                                              skos:altLabel "17_Statistical_Methods_For_Outcomes" ;
                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics ;
                                              rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                              rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStimulationTypeDetails
tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                  obo:IAO_0000112 "\"Manual stimulation applied to achieve De Qi; no electrical stimulation or moxibustion.\"" ,
                                                  "e.g., \"Manual manipulation to elicit de qi\" or \"Electroacupuncture at 2/100 Hz, 1-3 mA for 20 minutes.\"."@en ;
                                  dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                  dcterms:description "The type and parameters of stimulation applied to the inserted needles, such as manual manipulation or electroacupuncture settings."@en ;
                                  tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStimulationTypeDetails" ;
                                  rdfs:label "Stimulation Type Details" ;
                                  skos:altLabel "Stimulation_Type_Details" ;
                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                     tara-kb:hasAcupunctureProtocol ;
                                  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                  rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


