  \"field\": \"Studied_TCM_Condition\",
  \"description\": \"A dual-purpose annotation property that captures the raw, as-reported Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) condition or pattern-differentiation label from the article, while also serving as a super-property for its mapped, standardized counterpart (hasMappedTCMCondition).\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                               rdfs:label "Studied Condition (TCM)" ;
                               skos:altLabel "Studied_TCM_Condition" ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                  tara-kb:hasStudiedCondition ;
                               rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                               rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudiedWesternCondition
tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                   obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., \"Chronic Low Back Pain\" or \"Migraine without Aura\"."@en ;
                                   dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                   dcterms:description "A dual-purpose annotation property that captures the raw, as-reported Western/biomedical condition label from the article, while also serving as a super-property for its mapped, standardized counterpart (hasMappedWesternCondition)."@en ;
                                   tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudiedWesternCondition" ;
                                   tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Studied_Western_Condition\",
  \"description\": \"A dual-purpose annotation property that captures the raw, as-reported Western/biomedical condition label from the article, while also serving as a super-property for its mapped, standardized counterpart (hasMappedWesternCondition).\",
  \"normalization\": \"Extract the plain-language Western/biomedical condition studied, with no braces, parentheses, or bracketed abbreviations of any kind. If multiple conditions are combined into one compound phrase (e.g., 'neck and shoulder pain'), split into separate individual condition phrases (e.g., 'neck pain, shoulder pain') rather than keeping the compound form.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                   rdfs:label "Studied Condition (Western)" ;
                                   skos:altLabel "Studied_Western_Condition" ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                      tara-kb:hasStudiedCondition ;
                                   rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                   rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyConclusions
tara-kb:hasStudyConclusions rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                            obo:IAO_0000112 """e.g., \"Weak evidence was found of an effect of acupuncture on persistent non-specific low back pain at 12 months, but stronger evidence of a small benefit at 24 months. Referral to a qualified traditional acupuncturist for a short course of treatment seems safe and acceptable to patients with low back pain.\" 

The example above captures the \"Clinical Conclusions\" for the study 'Randomised controlled trial of a short course of traditional acupuncture compared with usual care for persistent non-specific low back pain'; Article DOI:https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.38878.907361.7C"""@en ;
                            dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                            dcterms:description "Captures a faithful summary of what the article reports as clinical conclusions, potentially including short direct quotations where appropriate."@en ;
                            tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyConclusions" ;
                            tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Study_Conclusions\",
  \"description\": \"Captures a faithful summary of what the article reports as clinical conclusions, potentially including short direct quotations where appropriate.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                            rdfs:comment """This field must not augment inferred \"Yes/No\" effectiveness statements.
Instead, the field should faithfully summarize what the paper reports as a clinical conclusion, potentially including short direct quotations where appropriate."""@en ;
                            rdfs:label "Study Conclusions" ;
                            skos:altLabel "Study_Conclusions" ;
                            rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                               tara-kb:hasStudyFindings ;
                            rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                            rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics
tara-kb:hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                         dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                         dcterms:description """Category C, Study Design and Analysis Metrics, groups the OCSI items describing how a trial was planned and how its analysis was designed. The OCSI items under this category include:
- Item 11: Outcomes Measure Definitions; 
- Item 12: Sample Size Determination; 
- Item 13: Random Allocation Sequencing;
- Item 14: Random Allocation Concealment;
- Item 15: Random Allocation Personnel; 
- Item 16: Blinding Statements Quality; and
- Item 17: Statistical Methods from Outcomes"""@en ;
                                         dcterms:type tara-kb:grouping ;
                                         tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyDesignAndAnalysisMetrics" ;
                                         tara-ap:hasSynonym "Trial Methodology and Analysis Planning Metrics" ;
                                         rdfs:comment "This category's members correspond closely to CONSORT's own Methods section (Outcomes, Sample size, Randomisation, Blinding, Statistical methods), distinguishing planned trial design and analysis content from the reported/executed content grouped under Category D."@en ;
                                         rdfs:label "Category C: Study Design & Analysis Metrics" ;
                                         skos:altLabel "Category_C_Study_Design_And_Analysis_Metrics" ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasOCSIItemScoringMetadata ;
                                         rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyDesignMetadata
tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                               dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                               dcterms:description "A grouping annotation property that organizes the sub-properties describing the study's design, comparator groups, sample retention, and treatment schedule."@en ;
                               dcterms:type tara-kb:grouping ;
                               tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata" ;
                               rdfs:label "Study Design Metadata" ;
                               skos:altLabel "Study_Design_Metadata" ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasAcupunctureStudyMetadata ;
                               rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyEffectiveness
tara-kb:hasStudyEffectiveness rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                              obo:IAO_0000112 """Example 1: \"Yes - acupuncture significantly reduced the duration of the active phase of labor and the need for oxytocin infusion compared to the control group.\"

Example 2: \"No - the primary outcome of reduction in migraine days did not differ significantly across the verum acupuncture, sham acupuncture, and standard therapy groups.\"

Example 2 above captures the inferred effectiveness detail based on the results and conclusions of the study 'Efficacy of acupuncture for the prophylaxis of migraine: a multicentre randomised controlled clinical trial'; PubMed link: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16545747"""@en ;
                              dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                              dcterms:description """Captures the final overall takeaway regarding the effectiveness of the treatment compared to the control group. It should be a focused statement on whether and how effective the studied intervention was, with clearly defined inference based solely on the information already extracted as Study Findings including Main Results and Clinical Conclusions or Comparative narrative. For example:
* Yes - A concise explanation of why the intervention was considered effective.
* No – A concise explanation of why the intervention was not considered effective.
* Inconclusive – A concise explanation of why the evidence is insufficient, mixed, or does not support a definitive conclusion."""@en ;
                              tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyEffectiveness" ;
                              tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Study_Effectiveness\",
  \"description\": \"Captures the final overall takeaway regarding the effectiveness of the treatment compared to the control group. It should be a focused statement on whether and how effective the studied intervention was, with clearly defined inference based solely on the information already extracted as Study Findings including Main Results and Clinical Conclusions or Comparative narrative. For example: * Yes - A concise explanation of why the intervention was considered effective. * No – A concise explanation of why the intervention was not considered effective. * Inconclusive – A concise explanation of why the evidence is insufficient, mixed, or does not support a definitive conclusion.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                              rdfs:label "Study Effectiveness" ;
                              skos:altLabel "Study_Effectiveness" ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyFindings ;
                              rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                              rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyFindings
tara-kb:hasStudyFindings rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                         obo:IAO_0000112 """\"Main Results: The primary outcome showed a mean reduction of 2·3 days (95% CI 1·9–2·7) in the verum acupuncture group, 1·5 days (1·1–2·0) in the sham acupuncture group, and 2·1 days (1·5–2·7) in the standard therapy group. These differences were statistically significant compared with baseline (p<0·0001), but not across the treatment groups (p=0·09).

Clinical Conclusions: Treatment outcomes for migraine do not differ between patients treated with sham acupuncture, verum acupuncture, or standard therapy.\"

The example above captures the study findings based on the results and conclusions from the study 'Efficacy of acupuncture for the prophylaxis of migraine: a multicentre randomised controlled clinical trial'; PubMed link: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16545747"""@en ;
                         dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                         dcterms:description """A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping the interpreted findings sub-properties (clinical conclusions, comparative findings, effectiveness, main results, and proposed mechanism), while simultaneously acting as a direct container for a general free-text stuctured summary of the study's findings when a more specific sub-property does not apply.

This field should faithfully summarize what the paper reports as main results (the core numeric and statistical information of the primary and secondary endpoints) and clinical conclusions in a structured way, potentially including short direct quotations where appropriate."""@en ;
                         tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyFindings" ;
                         tara-ap:hasSynonym "Study Outcomes" ;
                         rdfs:comment "In systematic reviews and clinical trial metadata, \"Findings\" or \"Conclusions\" are explicitly separated from raw outcome measures because they capture the interpreted results, statistical significance, and final takeaways of the research." ;
                         rdfs:label "Study Findings" ;
                         skos:altLabel "Study_Findings" ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasAcupunctureStudyMetadata ;
                         rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                         rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyID
tara-kb:hasStudyID rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                   dcterms:description "The Compact URI (CURIE) ID of a Research Study in TARA Articles KB." ;
                   tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyID" ;
                   rdfs:label "Has Study ID" ;
                   skos:altLabel "Study_ID" ;
                   rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:identifier ;
                   rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7008377> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyLocation
tara-kb:hasStudyLocation rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                         obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., \"Seoul National University Hospital, Seoul, South Korea\"."@en ;
                         dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                         dcterms:description "A dual-purpose annotation property that captures the general, as-reported location or site(s) where the trial was conducted, while also serving as a super-property for the normalized hasCountryOfStudy."@en ;
                         tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyLocation" ;
                         rdfs:label "Study Location" ;
                         skos:altLabel "Study_Location" ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ,
                                            tara-kb:hasAcupunctureStudyMetadata ;
                         rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                         rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt
tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                         obo:IAO_0000112 """{
  \"field\": \"Acupuncture_Protocol\",
  \"description\": \"A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping the granular acupuncture intervention sub-properties (method, needling, stimulation, sham, and acupoints), while simultaneously acting as a direct container for a single, structured free-text summary of the full acupuncture protocol. This field should conatin a structured summary combining acupoint selection and grouping, needling details, stimulation details, and sham protocol details into one field (see the 'example of usage' for full worked examples).\",
  \"normalization\": \"Produce one structured, uniformly-formatted entry combining four sub-parts, in this exact order and pipe-delimited format (see this property's own obo:IAO_0000112 for full worked examples): 'Point selection and grouping: <text> | Needling details: <text> | Stimulation details: <text> | Sham protocol details: <text>'. Base 'Point selection and grouping' on the context described for hasAcupointSelectionAndGrouping (the acupoints' selection rationale and grouping/combination logic) -- do NOT restate the raw acupoint list itself, which belongs under hasListedAcupoints only. Base 'Needling details' on the context described for hasNeedlingDetails, 'Stimulation details' on hasStimulationTypeDetails, and 'Sham protocol details' on hasShamAcupunctureDetails. If a sub-part is not reported, write 'Not specified' for that sub-part only, not for the whole entry. These four sub-parts are captured here only -- they are not extracted again as separate fields.\"
}"""@en ;
                                         dcterms:description """The compact, LLM-facing extraction fragment for a single Acupuncture Study Metadata field, attached directly to that field's property (e.g. hasAcupunctureProtocol). Combined by the extraction pipeline with hasGeneralStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt and the article's full text into one API call covering all Study Metadata fields at once.

Top-level JSON keys:

- 'field' -- the property's skos:altLabel (the spreadsheet column name).

- 'description' -- the field's meaning, taken directly from the property's own dcterms:description.

- 'normalization' -- present only where a field needs extraction/formatting guidance beyond the general rules in hasGeneralStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt (e.g. the structured multi-sub-part format required for hasAcupunctureProtocol, hasStudyOutcomesMeasure, and hasTreatmentDurationAndFrequency); absent otherwise."""@en ;
                                         rdfs:label "Study Metadata Extraction Prompt" ;
                                         skos:altLabel "Study_Metadata_Extraction_Prompt" ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasLLMExtractionPrompt ;
                                         rdfs:range rdf:JSON .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyOutcomesAndEffectSizeScore
tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesAndEffectSizeScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                           dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                           dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                           dcterms:description """The reporting quality score that assesses the completeness, transparency, and accuracy of the reported results for each predefined primary and secondary outcome measure, evaluating whether the text explicitly provides estimated effect sizes, confidence intervals, and precise statistical significance values (e.g., p-values) for each endpoint.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                           tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesAndEffectSizeScore" ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """For each primary and (if applicable) secondary outcome, is

(a) a summary of results presented for each group,

(b) the estimated effect size presented for each between-group difference (e.g., SD), and

(c) the precision of the effect size presented for each between-group difference (e.g., confidence interval (CI))?"""@en ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "22"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) It must state the results or use a table/graph, for example, the mean and standard deviation of the measurements.

(b) All results must indicate the effect size, for example, the difference in means, odds ratio, or relative risk ratio.

(c) For full credit, authors must state precision as a confidence interval (CI). Only presenting P-values will score a partial."""@en ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 22,
  \"question\": \"For each primary and (if applicable) secondary outcome, is (a) a summary of results presented for each group, (b) the estimated effect size presented for each between-group difference (e.g., SD), and (c) the precision of the effect size presented for each between-group difference (e.g., confidence interval (CI))?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"a summary of results is presented for each group, for each primary (and, if applicable, secondary) outcome\",
    \"b\": \"the estimated effect size is presented for each between-group difference\",
    \"c\": \"the precision of the effect size is presented as a confidence interval (CI) -- presenting only P-values does not satisfy this sub-part\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                           tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) a summary of results is presented for each group, for each primary (and, if applicable, secondary) outcome;

(b) the estimated effect size is presented for each between-group difference;

(c) the precision of the effect size is presented as a confidence interval (CI) -- presenting only P-values does not satisfy this sub-part.

N = 3 when all 3 are applicable.

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-c):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Any count strictly between 0 and N met -> Score 1 (Partial). This applies whether 1 of 3 or 2 of 3 sub-parts are met.

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011)."""@en ;
                                           tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Results"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                           rdfs:comment """To maintain data integrity and prevent construct contamination within the metadata schema, ensure that the data extraction models treat the following two properties separately:

1. hasOutcomesMeasureScore (Methodology/Design Check): Focuses on the definition and planned pairing of tests. (e.g., Did they tell us in the Methods section how they planned to calculate the math?)

2. hasStudyOutcomesEffectSize (Reporting/Transparency Check): Focuses on the execution and transparency of the actual data. (e.g., Did they actually show us the exact numbers, tables, effect sizes, and p-values in the Results section?)"""@en ;
                                           rdfs:label "(22) Study Outcomes & Effect Size" ;
                                           skos:altLabel "22_Study_Outcomes_Effect_Size" ;
                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasResultsAndOutcomesMetrics ;
                                           rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                           rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyOutcomesMeasure
tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                obo:IAO_0000112 """e.g., \"Primary outcome measure: Proportion of responders (defined as the proportion of patients with a reduction of migraine days by at least 50%).

Secondary outcome measures: Number of migraine days, visual analogue scale (VAS) for pain, physical and mental component summary scores of the 36-item short-form health survey (SF-36), change in migraine days, number of patients with acute medication, adverse events (AE).\""""@en ;
                                dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                dcterms:description """A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping the primary and secondary outcome measure sub-properties, while simultaneously acting as a direct container for structured oucome measures as \"Primary Outcome Measure\" and/or \"Secondary Outcome Measure\". 

This property can also be used to capture the general outcome measure for the studies where primary/secondary distinction is not reported or not applicable."""@en ;
                                tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyOutcomesMeasure" ;
                                tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Study_Outcomes_Measure\",
  \"description\": \"A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping the primary and secondary outcome measure sub-properties, while simultaneously acting as a direct container for structured oucome measures as \\\\\\\"Primary Outcome Measure\\\\\\\" and/or \\\\\\\"Secondary Outcome Measure\\\\\\\". This property can also be used to capture the general outcome measure for the studies where primary/secondary distinction is not reported or not applicable.\",
  \"normalization\": \"Produce one structured entry combining primary and secondary outcome measures, labeled explicitly, e.g. 'Primary outcome measure: <text>. Secondary outcome measures: <text>.' (see this property's own obo:IAO_0000112 for a full worked example). If the primary/secondary distinction is not reported or not applicable, describe the general outcome measure(s) instead without forcing the primary/secondary labels. These are captured together here only -- they are not extracted again as separate fields, because primary and secondary outcomes are often defined relative to each other and separating them loses that context.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                rdfs:label "Study Outcomes Measure" ;
                                skos:altLabel "Study_Outcomes_Measure" ;
                                rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                   tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata ;
                                rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyQualityAssessmentMetadata
tara-kb:hasStudyQualityAssessmentMetadata rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                          dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                          dcterms:description """An annotation property that serves as a high-level grouping property under which specific quality assessment properties are defined to record evaluative quality data, risk-of-bias scores, and methodological rigor metrics calculated for a clinical trial study.

- Crucially, the values asserted by the sub-properties under this property are not raw data elements directly extracted or verbatim copied from the published journal article. Instead, they represent secondary, derived assessment scores generated, either algorithmically by automated computational models or manually by human domain experts, by evaluating an extracted set of primary metadata from the study report against standardized scoring frameworks and quality assessment criteria (such as OCSI)."""@en ;
                                          dcterms:type tara-kb:grouping ;
                                          tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyQualityAssessmentMetadata" ;
                                          rdfs:label "Study Assessment Metadata"@en ;
                                          skos:altLabel "Study_Assessment_Metadata"@en ;
                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasTARAArticlesMetadata ;
                                          rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7227329> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyRationaleAndScopeMetrics
tara-kb:hasStudyRationaleAndScopeMetrics rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                         dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                         dcterms:description """Category A, Study Rationale and Scope Metrics, groups the OCSI items that establish why a trial was undertaken and what it covers before its methods and results are reported. The OCSI Items under this category include:
- Item 1: Participants Randomization Statement;
- Item 2: Scientific Background and Rationale; 
- Item 3: Participants Eligibility and Study Settings;
- Item 10: Specific Objectives and Hypotheses."""@en ;
                                         dcterms:type tara-kb:grouping ;
                                         tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyRationaleAndScopeMetrics" ;
                                         tara-ap:hasSynonym "Study Foundation and Background Metrics" ,
                                                            "Trial Framing and Background Metrics" ;
                                         rdfs:label "Category A: Study Rationale & Scope Metrics" ;
                                         skos:altLabel "Category_A_Study_Rationale_And_Scope_Metrics" ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasOCSIItemScoringMetadata ;
                                         rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyResults
tara-kb:hasStudyResults rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                        obo:IAO_0000112 """e.g., \"At 12 months average SF-36 pain scores increased by 33.2 to 64.0 in the acupuncture group and by 27.9 to 58.3 in the control group. Adjusting for baseline score and for any clustering by acupuncturist, the estimated intervention effect was 5.6 points (95% confidence interval − 0.2 to 11.4) at 12 months (n = 213) and 8.0 points (2.8 to 13.2) at 24 months (n = 182).\"

The example above captures the \"Main Results\" from the study 'Randomised controlled trial of a short course of traditional acupuncture compared with usual care for persistent non-specific low back pain'. Article DOI:https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.38878.907361.7C"""@en ;
                        dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                        dcterms:description "Captures the main results of the clinical trial containing numeric and statistical information of the primary and secondary endpoints."@en ;
                        tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyResults" ;
                        tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Study_Results\",
  \"description\": \"Captures the main results of the clinical trial containing numeric and statistical information of the primary and secondary endpoints.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                        rdfs:label "Study Results" ;
                        skos:altLabel "Study_Results" ;
                        rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                           tara-kb:hasStudyFindings ;
                        rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                        rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasStudyType
tara-kb:hasStudyType rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                     obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., \"Randomized Controlled Trial\", \"Crossover Trial\", \"Meta analysis\", \"Systematic Review\"."@en ;
                     dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                     dcterms:description "An annotation property that serves as a direct container for the high-level study type categorization (e.g., \"Randomized Controlled Trial\", \"Crossover Trial\", \"Meta Analysis\", \"Systemetic Review\" )."@en ;
                     tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasStudyType" ;
                     tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Study_Type\",
  \"description\": \"An annotation property that serves as a direct container for the high-level study type categorization (e.g., \\\"Randomized Controlled Trial\\\", \\\"Crossover Trial\\\", \\\"Meta Analysis\\\", \\\"Systemetic Review\\\" ).\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                     rdfs:label "Study Design Category" ;
                     skos:altLabel "Study_Type" ;
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:type ,
                                        tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata ;
                     rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                     rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasSubgroupAdjustedAnalysesScore
tara-kb:hasSubgroupAdjustedAnalysesScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                         dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                         dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                         dcterms:description """The structural quality score assessing the tracking of subgroups, post-hoc stratifications, or secondary data analyses of the clinical trial.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                         tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasSubgroupAdjustedAnalysesScore" ;
                                         tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions "If additional subgroup analyses and/or adjusted analyses are reported, is it stated whether they were prespecified or exploratory, that is, not prespecified?"@en ;
                                         tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "23"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                         tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions "If additional analyses are prespecified in the research design, the results must be presented, and it must be clearly stated whether or not these were exploratory (e.g., post hoc) analyses."@en ;
                                         tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 23,
  \"question\": \"If additional subgroup analyses and/or adjusted analyses are reported, is it stated whether they were prespecified or exploratory, that is, not prespecified?\",
  \"criteria\": {
    \"yes\": \"it is clearly stated whether the additional subgroup and/or adjusted analyses reported were prespecified or exploratory (e.g., post hoc).\",
    \"partial\": \"results of additional analyses are presented, but their prespecified/exploratory status is not clearly stated.\",
    \"no\": \"additional analyses are reported with no indication of prespecified/exploratory status, or status is stated without presenting results.\",
    \"na\": \"N/A if no additional subgroup or adjusted analyses were reported at all.\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                         tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """- Score 2 (Yes): it is clearly stated whether the additional subgroup and/or adjusted analyses reported were prespecified or exploratory (e.g., post hoc).

- Score 1 (Partial): results of additional analyses are presented, but their prespecified/exploratory status is not clearly stated.

- Score 0 (No): additional analyses are reported with no indication of prespecified/exploratory status, or status is stated without presenting results.

- N/A if no additional subgroup or adjusted analyses were reported at all."""@en ;
                                         tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Results"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                         rdfs:comment "" ;
                                         rdfs:label "(23) Subgroup & Adjusted Analyses" ;
                                         skos:altLabel "23_Subgroup_Adjusted_Analyses" ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasResultsAndOutcomesMetrics ;
                                         rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                         rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTARAArticlesMetadata
tara-kb:hasTARAArticlesMetadata rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                dcterms:description "A grouping annotation property to organize all metadata annotation properties specific to TARA articles knowledgebase." ;
                                dcterms:type tara-kb:grouping ;
                                tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasTARAArticlesMetadata" ;
                                tara-kb:hasGeneralArticleExtractionPrompt """{
  \"role\": \"You are extracting structured metadata from one full-text acupuncture clinical trial article into a predefined set of fields, guided by the TARA ontology.\",
  \"task\": \"Load this article's full text once and reuse it, with prompt caching, across three sequential extraction calls in this fixed order: (1) Bibliographic Metadata (see hasBibliographicMetadata's hasGeneralBibliographicMetadataExtractionPrompt), (2) Acupuncture Study Metadata (see hasAcupunctureStudyMetadata's hasGeneralStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt), (3) OCSI Score Data (see hasOCSIItemScoringMetadata's hasGeneralOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt, a sibling branch of this one, not a structural descendant -- consult it separately). Preserve the same Article_ID_Curie across all three outputs so the resulting spreadsheet rows can be joined.\",
  \"ontology_grounding\": \"For every field's meaning, expected format, and which spreadsheet column it maps to, the field's own hasBibliographicMetadataExtractionPrompt / hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt fragment (and its skos:altLabel) in the ontology are authoritative -- do not infer a field's meaning from its property name alone. If a field is not accompanied by an extraction-prompt fragment, it is a derived/mapped or organizational property and must not be extracted directly.\",
  \"response_format\": \"Each of the three extraction calls returns its own JSON object/array as specified in that call's own general prompt; this master prompt does not define a combined output shape.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                rdfs:label "TARA-KB: Articles Metadata" ;
                                skos:altLabel "TARA_KB_Articles_Metadata" .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTreatmentDuration
tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                             obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., \"6 weeks\", \"12 sessions over 1 month\"."@en ;
                             dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                             dcterms:description "Captures the information about the total length of the therapy course."@en ;
                             tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasTreatmentDuration" ;
                             rdfs:comment "For the total length of the therapy course (e.g., \"6 weeks\", \"12 sessions over 1 month\")." ;
                             rdfs:label "Treatment Duration" ;
                             skos:altLabel "Treatment_Duration" ;
                             rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                tara-kb:hasTreatmentDurationAndFrequency ;
                             rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                             rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTreatmentDurationAndFrequency
tara-kb:hasTreatmentDurationAndFrequency rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                         obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., \"12 sessions over 6 weeks, administered 2 times per week.\"."@en ;
                                         dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                         dcterms:description "A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping hasTreatmentDuration and hasTreatmentFrequency, while simultaneously acting as a direct container for a combined free-text statement of the treatment's duration and frequency."@en ;
                                         tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasTreatmentDurationAndFrequency" ;
                                         tara-kb:hasStudyMetadataExtractionPrompt """{
  \"field\": \"Treatment_Duration_And_Frequency\",
  \"description\": \"A dual-purpose annotation property that serves as a super-property grouping hasTreatmentDuration and hasTreatmentFrequency, while simultaneously acting as a direct container for a combined free-text statement of the treatment's duration and frequency.\",
  \"normalization\": \"Produce one combined statement of both the treatment's duration (total length of the treatment course) and frequency (how often sessions occurred), e.g. '12 sessions over 6 weeks, administered 2 times per week.' Duration and frequency are captured together here only -- they are not extracted again as separate fields, because they are typically reported together and separating them loses that context.\"
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                         rdfs:label "Treatment Duration and Frequency" ;
                                         skos:altLabel "Treatment_Duration_And_Frequency" ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata ;
                                         rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                         rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTreatmentFrequency
tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                              obo:IAO_0000112 "e.g., \"3 times per week\", \"Every other day\"."@en ;
                              dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                              dcterms:description "Captures the information about how often the intervention was administered."@en ;
                              tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasTreatmentFrequency" ;
                              rdfs:comment "For how often the intervention was administered (e.g., \"3 times per week\", \"Every other day\")." ;
                              rdfs:label "Treatment Frequency" ;
                              skos:altLabel "Treatment_Frequency" ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                 tara-kb:hasTreatmentDurationAndFrequency ;
                              rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                              rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6701896> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTreatmentsDurationAndFrequencyScore
tara-kb:hasTreatmentsDurationAndFrequencyScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                               dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                               dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                               dcterms:description """The STRICTA-aligned reporting item score checking if treatment intervals, session patterns, and total schedules are documented.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                               tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasTreatmentsDurationAndFrequencyScore" ;
                                               tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """(a) Are the number and

(b) frequency of treatments stated?"""@en ;
                                               tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "6"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                               tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) If treatments were individualized, then the mean and range of the number of treatments must be stated.

(b) If the protocol was one treatment, then the frequency is N/A."""@en ;
                                               tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 6,
  \"question\": \"(a) Are the number and (b) frequency of treatments stated?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"the number of treatments is stated\",
    \"b\": \"the frequency of treatments is stated (N/A if the protocol was a single treatment.)\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                               tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) the number of treatments is stated;

(b) the frequency of treatments is stated.

N = 2 when all 2 are applicable; N is reduced by however many sub-parts are individually N/A (see below).

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-b):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Exactly 1 of N met -> Score 1 (Partial).

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011).

Sub-part N/A conditions:

(b) is N/A if the protocol was a single treatment."""@en ;
                                               tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Methods"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                               rdfs:label "(6) Treatments Duration & Frequency" ;
                                               skos:altLabel "6_Treatments_Duration_Frequency" ;
                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasAcupunctureInterventionMetrics ;
                                               rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                               rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTrialGeneralizabilityScore
tara-kb:hasTrialGeneralizabilityScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                      dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                      dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                      dcterms:description """The reporting quality score assessing whether the generalizability (external validity) of the trial findings is discussed.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                      tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasTrialGeneralizabilityScore" ;
                                      tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions "Is the generalizability (external validity) of the trial findings discussed?"@en ;
                                      tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "26"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                      tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions "Generalizability pertains to the external validity or general applicability of the results. For example, to what extent do the results, with the population limited by the eligibility criteria, pertain to the greater population with this condition? Topics to consider are eligibility criteria, setting and location, the intervention protocol, the period of recruitment and followup, and so forth."@en ;
                                      tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 26,
  \"question\": \"Is the generalizability (external validity) of the trial findings discussed?\",
  \"criteria\": {
    \"yes\": \"the generalizability (external validity) of the trial findings is discussed, considering topics such as eligibility criteria, setting and location, the intervention protocol, and the period of recruitment and follow-up.\",
    \"partial\": \"generalizability is briefly mentioned without substantive discussion of the topics above.\",
    \"no\": \"generalizability of the findings is not discussed.\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                      tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """- Score 2 (Yes): the generalizability (external validity) of the trial findings is discussed, considering topics such as eligibility criteria, setting and location, the intervention protocol, and the period of recruitment and follow-up.

- Score 1 (Partial): (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011) generalizability is briefly mentioned without substantive discussion of the topics above.

- Score 0 (No): generalizability of the findings is not discussed."""@en ;
                                      tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Discussion"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                      rdfs:label "(26) Trial Findings Generalizability" ;
                                      skos:altLabel "26_Trial_Findings_Generalizability" ;
                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasResultsDiscussionMetrics ;
                                      rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                      rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTrialStrengthsLimitationsScore
tara-kb:hasTrialStrengthsLimitationsScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                          dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Hammerschlag R, Milley RJ, Colbert A, Weih J, Yohalem-Ilsley B, Mist S, Aickin M. Randomized Controlled Trials of Acupuncture (1997–2007): An Assessment of Reporting Quality with a CONSORT- and STRICTA-Based Instrument. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2011. https://doi.org/10.1155/2011/183910"@en ;
                                          dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                          dcterms:description """The reporting quality score evaluating whether the study authors adequately identified and discussed the strengths and weaknesses of the trial such as potential sources of bias or other trial constraints.

- The OCSI Item Number, Assessment Question(s) (reproduced from Table 1, Hammerschlag et al., 2011),  and Per Question Instructions(s) (reproduced from Appendix A.2, Hammerschlag et al., 2011) are reproduced under the CC-BY license, with attribution to the original authors. See the Bibliographic Citation section."""@en ;
                                          tara-ap:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasTrialStrengthsLimitationsScore" ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIAssessmentQuestions """Is an interpretation of the results presented that takes into account

(a) study hypotheses,

(b) sources of potential bias or imprecision, and

(c) the potential dangers associated with multiple analyses and outcomes?"""@en ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIItemNumber "25"^^tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIPerQuestionInstructions """(a) The relevance of the findings to the hypotheses or objectives must be discussed.

(b) The strengths and weakness of the trial must be discussed, particularly in the context of potential for bias and imprecision of study findings.

(c) This is usually scored as N/A unless numerous analyses, both prespecified and exploratory, were performed."""@en ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIScoreExtractionPrompt """{
  \"item\": 25,
  \"question\": \"Is an interpretation of the results presented that takes into account (a) study hypotheses, (b) sources of potential bias or imprecision, and (c) the potential dangers associated with multiple analyses and outcomes?\",
  \"parts\": {
    \"a\": \"the interpretation addresses the study hypotheses\",
    \"b\": \"the interpretation addresses sources of potential bias or imprecision\",
    \"c\": \"the interpretation addresses the potential dangers associated with multiple analyses and outcomes (usually N/A unless numerous analyses, both prespecified and exploratory, were performed.)\"
  }
}"""^^rdf:JSON ;
                                          tara-kb:hasOCSIScoringRubric """Applicable sub-parts:

(a) the interpretation addresses the study hypotheses;

(b) the interpretation addresses sources of potential bias or imprecision;

(c) the interpretation addresses the potential dangers associated with multiple analyses and outcomes.

N = 3 when all 3 are applicable; N is reduced by however many sub-parts are individually N/A (see below).

Combination rule (N = applicable sub-parts among a-c):

- All N met -> Score 2 (Yes).

- 0 of N met -> Score 0 (No).

- Any count strictly between 0 and N met -> Score 1 (Partial). This applies whether 1 of 3 or 2 of 3 sub-parts are met.

OCSI's scale has no graduated partial; any mix short of full or zero collapses to the same Score 1.

- If all applicable sub-parts are N/A -> item scored N/A (interpretive extension, not explicit in Hammerschlag et al. 2011).

Sub-part N/A conditions:

(c) is usually N/A unless numerous analyses, both prespecified and exploratory, were performed."""@en ;
                                          tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection "Discussion"^^tara-kb:articleSectionType ;
                                          rdfs:label "(25) Trial Strengths & Limitations" ;
                                          skos:altLabel "25_Trial_Strengths_Limitations" ;
                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasResultsDiscussionMetrics ;
                                          rdfs:range tara-kb:ocsiItemScore ;
                                          rdfs:domain <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2825659> .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasTypicalArticleSection
tara-kb:hasTypicalArticleSection rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                 dcterms:description "The structural section of a published article (per Table 1, Hammerschlag et al. 2011) in which the information needed to answer this OCSI item is conventionally reported; e.g., Abstract, Introduction, Methods, Results, or Discussion. This documents where the information is typically found, not a strict extraction-location requirement: per OCSI's general scoring instructions, information located anywhere in the document may still receive full credit, with the sole exception of item 1, which must specifically appear in the Abstract or Title."@en ;
                                 rdfs:label "Typical Article Section" ;
                                 skos:altLabel "Typical_Article_Section" ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation ;
                                 rdfs:range tara-kb:articleSectionType .


###  http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment
rdfs:comment rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label
rdfs:label rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso
rdfs:seeAlso rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated
owl:deprecated rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel
skos:altLabel rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
              rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:skosAnntotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hiddenLabel
skos:hiddenLabel rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-ap:skosAnntotationProperty .


#################################################################
#    Datatypes
#################################################################

###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/articleSectionType
tara-kb:articleSectionType rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                           dcterms:description "An enumerated custom datatype that restricts allowed values to standard structural sections of a scientific or academic article (e.g., Abstract, Introduction, Methods, Results, Discussion, Conclusion, References, Tables, Figures). It is intended for use with annotation properties to categorize the specific structural context of text fragments or article components without requiring an OWL class structure."@en ;
                           rdfs:label "Datatype: Article Section"@en ;
                           owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                                 owl:oneOf [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                             rdf:first "Abstract" ;
                                                             rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                        rdf:first "Conclusion" ;
                                                                        rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                   rdf:first "Discussion" ;
                                                                                   rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                              rdf:first "Figures" ;
                                                                                              rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                                         rdf:first "Introduction" ;
                                                                                                         rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                                                    rdf:first "Methods" ;
                                                                                                                    rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                                                               rdf:first "References" ;
                                                                                                                               rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                                                                          rdf:first "Results" ;
                                                                                                                                          rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                                                                                     rdf:first "Tables" ;
                                                                                                                                                     rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                                                                                                rdf:first "Title" ;
                                                                                                                                                                rdf:rest rdf:nil
                                                                                                                                                              ]
                                                                                                                                                   ]
                                                                                                                                        ]
                                                                                                                             ]
                                                                                                                  ]
                                                                                                       ]
                                                                                            ]
                                                                                 ]
                                                                      ]
                                                           ]
                                               ] .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/ocsiItemNumber
tara-kb:ocsiItemNumber rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                       dcterms:description "The standard item number (1-27) in the Oregon CONSORT STRICTA Instrument (OCSI)."@en ;
                       rdfs:label "Datatype: OCSI Item Number" ;
                       owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                             owl:onDatatype xsd:short ;
                                             owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive "1"^^xsd:short
                                                                    ]
                                                                    [ xsd:maxInclusive "27"^^xsd:short
                                                                    ]
                                                                  )
                                           ] .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/ocsiItemScore
tara-kb:ocsiItemScore rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                      rdfs:comment "The valid per-item OCSI score: 0 (no), 1 (partial), 2 (yes), or the string 'N/A' when the item does not apply. Per Hammerschlag et al. 2011, each of the 27 OCSI questions is scored yes = 2, partial = 1, no = 0, or Not Applicable = N/A."@en ;
                      rdfs:label "Datatype: OCSI Item Score" ;
                      owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                            owl:unionOf ( [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                                            owl:oneOf [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                        rdf:first 0 ;
                                                                        rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                   rdf:first 1 ;
                                                                                   rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                              rdf:first 2 ;
                                                                                              rdf:rest rdf:nil
                                                                                            ]
                                                                                 ]
                                                                      ]
                                                          ]
                                                          [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                                            owl:oneOf [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                        rdf:first "N/A" ;
                                                                        rdf:rest rdf:nil
                                                                      ]
                                                          ]
                                                        )
                                          ] .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/ocsiItemScoreRequired
tara-kb:ocsiItemScoreRequired rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                              rdfs:comment "The valid per-item OCSI score for items that cannot be scored N/A: 0 (no), 1 (partial), or 2 (yes). Per Hammerschlag et al. 2011, item 24 (adverse events) is the sole exception to the general N/A allowance -- 'It cannot be scored as N/A.'"@en ;
                              rdfs:label "Datatype: OCSI Item Score Required" ;
                              owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                                    owl:oneOf [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                rdf:first 0 ;
                                                                rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                           rdf:first 1 ;
                                                                           rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                                      rdf:first 2 ;
                                                                                      rdf:rest rdf:nil
                                                                                    ]
                                                                         ]
                                                              ]
                                                  ] .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/percentFloat
tara-kb:percentFloat rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                     rdfs:comment """To represent the total OCSI Score percentage between 0.0 to 100.0. 

The global reporting-quality percentage for a study's OCSI assessment, calculated per Hammerschlag et al. 2011 as: raw score / (2 x [27 - n items scored N/A]) x 100."""@en ;
                     rdfs:label "Datatype: OCSI Total Score" ;
                     owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                           owl:onDatatype xsd:float ;
                                           owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive "0.0"^^xsd:float
                                                                  ]
                                                                  [ xsd:maxInclusive "100.0"^^xsd:float
                                                                  ]
                                                                )
                                         ] .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/propertyType
tara-kb:propertyType rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                     dcterms:description "The type of the annotation or object property to restrict its use as grouping, value holding, grouping and value-holding. Grouping indicates that the property serves as an organizational super property of its sub-properties."@en ;
                     rdfs:label "Property Type"@en ;
                     owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                           owl:oneOf [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                       rdf:first "Grouping" ;
                                                       rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                  rdf:first "Grouping or Value-Holding" ;
                                                                  rdf:rest [ rdf:type rdf:List ;
                                                                             rdf:first "Value-Holding" ;
                                                                             rdf:rest rdf:nil
                                                                           ]
                                                                ]
                                                     ]
                                         ] .


###  http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#JSON
rdf:JSON rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .


###  http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear
xsd:gYear rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .


